# Clause IDs a document deliberately names although the active constitution does
# not declare them. One `ID — reason` per line; `#` comments allowed.
#
# Read by `docs_link_guard::tests::every_clause_id_in_prose_resolves`. Prefer
# rewording over an entry: a clause ID in prose is a promise a reader can look it
# up. An entry belongs here only when the document's *subject* is a clause that
# is not in force — a reserved ID, or a fabricated one shown as a counterexample.
#
# Unlike `.link-guard-allow`, entries here are expected to expire: when a
# reserved ID is enacted it leaves this file, and when the prose discussing a
# counterexample is archived the entry goes with it.

